Let's take the actionButton("takesample","Echantillonner") for exemple. If i want this button to be in both tabs "Vue graphique" et "Données", i can't just copy paste this actionButton declaration in both tabs, because it will work only when i click on the first declared, ie the one in the first tab, because they have the same id, wich have to be unique.

Then i must declare this actionButton twice, with 2 different ids : actionButton("takesample0","Echantillonner") in first tab, actionButton("takesample1","Echantillonner") in second tab, and update server.R to test not only input$takesample but both input$takesample0 and input$takesample1 to get samples to be genereted from both tabs. And so on if I want more than two tabs.
Maybe I will inspire myself from your exemple to set theses actionButtons as lists actionButton("takesample[[0]]","Echantillonner"), actionButton("takesample[[1]]","Echantillonner"), and program test on value independtly to number of actionButton of this kind of id... I will try, and come back if find an elegant solution.

Grégoire

